# Description
This one is kind of funny actually because of the webpage we are given to inspect.
We are told to use web inspect on the given webpage that has two other pages that are on it in order to find the flag.

# Solution
URL: http://titan.picoctf.net:60527/index.html
We are given this url. It shows an image of a guy in glasses smiling and text saying "Ha!!!!!! You looking for a flag?
Keep Navigating

Haaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa

Keepppppppppppppp Searchinggggggggggggggggggg"
I inspected the page's html code to find anything useful but on the home page, there was no flag and nothing in the element that was useful. So i inspected the next page the "about me" page.
About me URL: http://titan.picoctf.net:60527/about.html
The text in the url said "Try inspecting the page!! You might find it there". I inspected the element and found this in the code "notify_true="cGljb0NURnt3ZWJfc3VjYzNzc2Z1bGx5X2QzYzBkZWRfMTBmOTM3NmZ9"" which looked like base64.
What I did was use the provided webshell from picoctf to use the following command:
echo "cGljb0NURnt3ZWJfc3VjYzNzc2Z1bGx5X2QzYzBkZWRfMTBmOTM3NmZ9" | base64 -d
this allowed me to decipher the string and gave me the flag

